From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:38:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Embedding: an instruction that faults has changed nothing

The embedding host resolves a guest page fault, a copy-on-write store
among them, and runs the faulting instruction again from the state the
fault left, so that state must be the one the instruction found. Some
instructions changed state before their last access could fault:

- A read-modify-write wrote the flags before its store found the page
  read-only, so ADC, SBB, RCL and RCR ran again with the carry they
  had computed. The backend now finds each load whose bytes a store of
  the same instruction writes and translates it with
  EMBEDDER_ACCESS_READ_WRITE, so the write fault, or the end of a unit
  that stores into its own code, comes at the load.
- POP to memory updated RSP before its store. The store now comes
  first, its address formed from a node of its own.
- FLDENV, FRSTOR, FXRSTOR, XRSTOR and IRET loaded state from the first
  part of their operand before a later part faulted, and FLDENV did
  not read all of it. A new EmbedderProbe op faults as a load of the
  whole operand would, and each of them probes its operand first.
